                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is a core one for the collaboration between laboratory medicine and clinical practice, adopting a "theory + internship" model. It covers: (1) General principles of laboratory diagnostics, integration of laboratory testing with scientific research, and medical paper writing; (2) Laboratory safety and quality control; (3) Communication skills for various laboratory sub-specialties; (4) Practical laboratory operations and emergency testing practice.</p>
<p>Through this course, students will master core laboratory medicine theories and communication logic, become familiar with safety and quality control standards, acquire practical operation abilities and awareness of laboratory-clinical collaboration, and improve the accuracy of laboratory services.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
